description:
Edit TWO files in repos/development-vessel. FOUR string replacements total — two in each file. Change nothing else.

An empty-string env var defeats the `??` default: `??` falls back only on null/undefined, never on "". The repo already has the fix helper: `env(key, fallback)` in src/config.ts treats an empty/whitespace-only value as absent. Both files already import from ../config.js, so each import line only needs widening.

FILE 1 — repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/docs-align-tick.ts

EDIT 1 — replace this exact existing line:

import { METABOB_ENDPOINT } from "../config.js";

with:

import { METABOB_ENDPOINT, env } from "../config.js";

EDIT 2 — replace this exact existing line:

    const base = (process.env["DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT"] ?? "http://127.0.0.1:8100").replace(/\/+$/, "");

with:

    const base = env("DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT", "http://127.0.0.1:8100").replace(/\/+$/, "");

FILE 2 — repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/perf-canary-resolve.ts

EDIT 3 — replace this exact existing line:

import { METABOB_API_KEY } from "../config.js";

with:

import { METABOB_API_KEY, env } from "../config.js";

EDIT 4 — replace this exact existing line:

const DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT = process.env["DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT"] ?? "http://127.0.0.1:8100";

with:

const DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT = env("DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT", "http://127.0.0.1:8100");

Do not touch METABOB_API_KEY or any other env read: an API key is not an endpoint, and an empty key is a legitimate "no credential".

The change must typecheck (bun run lint). VERIFY BY CONSEQUENCE: with DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT exported as the empty string, both files resolve the discovery endpoint to "http://127.0.0.1:8100" rather than "", so their requests reach the discovery vessel instead of a relative path.

